e-ethics walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the two dilemma analyses authored and self-reviewed in-session
against the ISC2 Code of Ethics page (isc2.org/ethics, fetched 2026-10-10 via
browser_open after curl was bot-walled with a 403).

Scope: fictional Northwind Freight (300-person logistics; independent-consultant
engagement). Dilemmas: (A) out-of-scope critical VPN flaw the client is "aware"
of — argued Canon I (infrastructure) + Canon II (honesty by omission) outrank
the Canon-III-as-obedience reading; decision: formal written notice to the
sponsor, documented. (B) client pressure to downgrade a critical portal finding
before a prospect's due diligence — Canon II dispositive; Canon III's "service"
does not cover deceiving a third party; decision: refuse in writing, offer
expedited retest + documented risk acceptance. Both analyses name the decision
and its cost.

